# Role
You are writing the onboarding API route for TinyWins — the persistence
layer between the onboarding quiz UI and the trait engine.

# Requirements
Build `src/app/api/onboarding/route.ts` with two handlers:

**`GET`** — looks up the demo user's `UserTraits` row. Returns
`{ completed: false }` if none exists yet, otherwise
`{ completed: true, traits: TraitsProfile }`.

**`POST`** — body is `OnboardingRequest` (age, gender, optional
habitToImprove, optional newHabitGoal, optional base64 visionBoardImage,
required mood):
1. Validate `age` is a number between 13 and 120 — 400 if not.
2. Validate `mood` is one of the five allowed values — 400 if not.
3. If `visionBoardImage` is present, reject anything over ~2MB decoded
   with 400 (`"image too large"`) before touching the LLM — SQLite storage
   and LLM payload size are both good reasons to cap this early.
4. Call `buildInitialTraits` from `traits.ts` for the base profile.
5. If an image was provided and passed size validation, call
   `analyzeVisionBoard` and merge its `themes` into the profile; if that
   call fails internally it already returns `{ themes: [] }` per its own
   contract, so this route does not need its own try/catch around it.
6. Upsert (not create) the `UserTraits` row for the demo user — resubmitting
   onboarding updates the existing profile rather than erroring or
   duplicating.
7. Create a `MoodCheckIn` row for today with the submitted mood.
8. Return `{ traits: TraitsProfile }`.

# Interface
Reference `OnboardingRequest`, `TraitsProfile`, and `OnboardingResponse` —
these need to be added to `src/lib/contract.ts` (see below) before this
route can be generated; add them there first and get sign-off from all
three of you, since that file is the frozen team contract.

```ts
// contract.ts additions this route depends on
export type Mood = "rough" | "low" | "okay" | "good" | "great";

export interface OnboardingRequest {
  age: number;
  gender: string;
  habitToImprove?: string;
  newHabitGoal?: string;
  visionBoardImage?: string; // base64 data URL
  mood: Mood;
}

export interface OnboardingResponse {
  traits: TraitsProfile;
}

export interface OnboardingStatusResponse {
  completed: boolean;
  traits?: TraitsProfile;
}
```

# Dependencies
<include>src/lib/traits.ts</include>
<include>src/lib/prisma.ts</include>

# Acceptance criteria
- Age outside [13, 120] → 400, no DB write.
- Missing/invalid `mood` → 400, no DB write.
- Oversized image → 400 before any LLM call is made.
- Submitting onboarding twice updates the same `UserTraits` row (upsert),
  never creates a second one for the demo user.
- Every successful POST also creates exactly one `MoodCheckIn` row for
  that day.
